# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orbit — Telephony (Exotel)
#
# Copy the vars you need into your main .env to switch Orbit's /calls
# module from MOCK mode (every click-to-call returns a deterministic mock
# call sid — safe for dev/demos) to LIVE calls via Exotel's Call Connect API
# and inbound/outbound call event webhooks.
#
# See lib/telephony.ts (TELEPHONY_SETUP_DOC) for the full walkthrough and the
# exact request/response JSON shapes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Exotel Account SID (also the API Key / Basic-auth user for the Call Connect API).
# Find it at Dashboard → API Settings.
# EXOTEL_SID=your-exotel-account-sid

# Exotel API Token (Basic-auth password for the Call Connect API).
# Find it at Dashboard → API Settings.
# EXOTEL_TOKEN=your-exotel-api-token

# Your Exotel virtual number (the CallerId shown to the person being called,
# and the default "From" when a user's personal phone number isn't set).
# In E.164 format.
# EXOTEL_PHONE=+91XXXXXXXXXX

# Required for app/api/webhooks/telephony to do anything. Shared secret
# compared timing-safe against the `?token=` query param Exotel appends when
# it calls your webhook URL:
#   https://<your-domain>/api/webhooks/telephony?token=<this value>
# Without it the webhook route returns 503 and call events never advance
# past their initial status.
# TELEPHONY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── Where to get credentials ──
# 1. Sign up / log in at https://my.exotel.com and open the Dashboard.
# 2. Dashboard → API Settings → copy the Account SID + API Token + virtual number.
# 3. Create a call flow / Passthru applet that points to your webhook URL above.
# 4. Register the Passthru applet's outbound events to call:
#    https://<your-orbit-host>/api/webhooks/telephony?token=<TELEPHONY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN>
#    Exotel will hit this on every call event (queued, ringing, answered, completed,
#    busy, no-answer, failed, etc.) with call fields as query params.
# 5. Rotate TELEPHONY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN by updating its value here and in the
#    Passthru applet's webhook URL.
